{
  "id": "uo65ohw",
  "title": "CHAPTER 4: COMPUTER NETWORKS",
  "order": 4,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "iqorqpj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.1 OSI Reference Model"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The OSI Reference Model structures network communication into 7 distinct layers: Physical, Data Link, Network, Transport, Session, Presentation, and Application.",
        "TCP provides connection-oriented, reliable data transfer with error checking, whereas UDP offers fast, connectionless, unreliable transmission.",
        "IPv4 uses 32-bit addresses divided into 5 classes (A to E), whereas IPv6 provides 128-bit hexadecimal addresses to eliminate address exhaustion.",
        "Subnetting and Classless Inter-Domain Routing (CIDR) enable efficient IP allocation and reduced routing table size.",
        "Core network devices operate at specific OSI layers: Hubs (Layer 1), Switches (Layer 2), and Routers (Layer 3)."
      ],
      "id": "27w9r5o"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "OSI Layers",
          "value": "7 Layers",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "TCP/IP Layers",
          "value": "4 Layers",
          "icon": "check"
        },
        {
          "label": "IPv4 Address Length",
          "value": "32 Bits",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "IPv6 Address Length",
          "value": "128 Bits",
          "icon": "award"
        }
      ],
      "id": "iz2x07t"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "025m0xa",
      "content": "The OSI (Open Systems Interconnection) model is a conceptual framework with 7 layers used to standardise communication between different computer systems. Each layer provides services to the layer above and uses services from the layer below."
    },
    {
      "id": "nhgn29g",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Layer (Top to Bottom)</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Number</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Protocol Data Unit</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Key Protocols / Functions</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Application</p>",
            "<p>7</p>",
            "<p>Data (Message)</p>",
            "<p>HTTP, HTTPS, FTP, SMTP, DNS, DHCP, Telnet, SSH, SNMP</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Presentation</p>",
            "<p>6</p>",
            "<p>Data</p>",
            "<p>Encryption (SSL/TLS), compression, format conversion (JPEG, ASCII, EBCDIC)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Session</p>",
            "<p>5</p>",
            "<p>Data</p>",
            "<p>Session establishment, maintenance, termination; NetBIOS, RPC, SQL sessions</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Transport</p>",
            "<p>4</p>",
            "<p>Segment</p>",
            "<p>TCP (reliable), UDP (unreliable); port numbers; flow control; error control</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Network</p>",
            "<p>3</p>",
            "<p>Packet</p>",
            "<p>IP (IPv4, IPv6), ICMP, ARP, OSPF, BGP; routing; logical addressing</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Data Link</p>",
            "<p>2</p>",
            "<p>Frame</p>",
            "<p>MAC addressing; Ethernet, Wi-Fi (802.11); switches; error detection (CRC); HDLC, PPP</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Physical</p>",
            "<p>1</p>",
            "<p>Bits</p>",
            "<p>Physical transmission; cables, fibre, radio; hub, repeater; NIC; encoding</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eomrvn9",
      "content": "<strong>Note: </strong><em>Mnemonic for OSI layers (top to bottom): All People Seem To Need Data Processing. Or bottom to top: Please Do Not Throw Sausage Pizza Away.</em>"
    },
