    {
      "id": "yuaj9lc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.7 Network Devices"
    },
    {
      "id": "1qu3gm5",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Device</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>OSI Layer</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Function</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Key Difference</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hub</p>",
            "<p>Physical (L1)</p>",
            "<p>Broadcasts signal to all ports; dumb device</p>",
            "<p>No intelligence; creates collision domain</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Repeater</p>",
            "<p>Physical (L1)</p>",
            "<p>Regenerates/amplifies signal; extends cable distance</p>",
            "<p>Signal regeneration only</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Bridge</p>",
            "<p>Data Link (L2)</p>",
            "<p>Connects two network segments; uses MAC addresses; filters traffic</p>",
            "<p>Reduces collision domains</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Switch</p>",
            "<p>Data Link (L2)</p>",
            "<p>Connects multiple devices; uses MAC address table; unicast forwarding</p>",
            "<p>Each port = separate collision domain</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Router</p>",
            "<p>Network (L3)</p>",
            "<p>Routes packets between different networks; uses IP addresses; separates broadcast domains</p>",
            "<p>Works at layer 3; connects different networks</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Gateway</p>",
            "<p>Application (L7)</p>",
            "<p>Protocol conversion; connects networks with different architectures</p>",
            "<p>Full protocol translation</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Firewall</p>",
            "<p>Multiple Layers</p>",
            "<p>Filters traffic based on rules; stateful/stateless inspection</p>",
            "<p>Security device; packet filtering/inspection</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Load Balancer</p>",
            "<p>L4/L7</p>",
            "<p>Distributes traffic across multiple servers</p>",
            "<p>Availability and scalability</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Access Point (AP)</p>",
            "<p>Data Link (L2)</p>",
            "<p>Wireless connectivity; bridges wired and wireless LAN</p>",
            "<p>802.11 wireless; connects to switch</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Modem</p>",
            "<p>Physical (L1)</p>",
            "<p>Modulates/demodulates signal; converts digital to analog</p>",
            "<p>Required for DSL/cable internet access</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "zxhychs",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.8 Network Topologies"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "OSI vs TCP/IP layer mapping is highly tested: TCP/IP combines the Application, Presentation, and Session layers of OSI into a single Application layer.",
        "Memorize well-known port numbers: HTTP (80), HTTPS (443), FTP (20/21), DNS (53), Telnet (23), and SSH (22).",
        "Classful IPv4 ranges: Class A (1-126), Class B (128-191), Class C (192-223). Loopback address is 127.0.0.1.",
        "Distinguish Routing Protocols: RIP uses distance-vector (hop count limit 15), while OSPF uses link-state (Shortest Path First algorithm)."
      ],
      "id": "qy2e1w2"
    },
    {
      "id": "duhu6fq",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Topology</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Structure</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Advantages</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Disadvantages</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Bus</p>",
            "<p>All nodes on single cable</p>",
            "<p>Simple; cheap; easy to install</p>",
            "<p>Single point of failure; limited length; collision</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Ring</p>",
            "<p>Nodes connected in circular chain</p>",
            "<p>Equal access; no collisions (token ring)</p>",
            "<p>Single break disrupts all; difficult to troubleshoot</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Star</p>",
            "<p>All nodes connect to central hub/switch</p>",
            "<p>Easy to manage; one failure doesn't affect others</p>",
            "<p>Central device = single point of failure</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mesh</p>",
            "<p>Every node connected to every other node</p>",
            "<p>Highly redundant; no single failure point</p>",
            "<p>Expensive; complex; many cables</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Tree (Hierarchical)</p>",
            "<p>Combination of bus and star; branched</p>",
            "<p>Scalable; easy to extend</p>",
            "<p>Central hub failure affects many</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hybrid</p>",
            "<p>Combination of two or more topologies</p>",
            "<p>Flexible; combines advantages</p>",
            "<p>Complex design and management</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4ydshvp",
